.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS "RFC 4716 public key files"
.PP
"\-\-\-\- BEGIN SSH2 PUBLIC KEY \-\-\-\-", headers ("Subject:" and "Comment:" are understood and the others ignored; a value may continue on the next line after a backslash), the key blob in base64, and the END line.  This is what ssh\-keygen \-e writes by default.  Certificates are refused.  If COMMENT is not NULL it receives the Comment header (up to CAP bytes, NUL terminated, quotes removed), else "".
.TP
int \fBgf_key_from_rfc4716\fP (gf_key **out, const char *text, size_t len, char *comment, size_t cap);
.TP
int \fBgf_key_to_rfc4716\fP (const gf_key *key, const char *comment, char *out, size_t cap, size_t *len);
The file for KEY, with a Comment header if COMMENT is not NULL.  Lines are as ssh\-keygen \-e makes them.  OUT is NUL\-terminated; *LEN receives its length without the NUL.
.SS "PEM"
.PP
.nf
.RS
One PEM block whose label is
  PUBLIC KEY             an SPKI (what openssl pkey \-pubout writes)
  RSA PUBLIC KEY         a PKCS#1 RSAPublicKey
  PRIVATE KEY            PKCS#8, unencrypted (also its version 2 form
                         with the public key in it)
  ENCRYPTED PRIVATE KEY  PKCS#8 under PBES2: PBKDF2 with SHA\-256, \-384 or
                         \-512 and AES\-128, \-192 or \-256 in CBC mode, with
                         at most 5,000,000 iterations
  RSA PRIVATE KEY        PKCS#1
  EC PRIVATE KEY         SEC1, which must carry the public point
The private forms of ECDSA must carry the public point (every writer
does); an Ed25519 key's public key is computed from its seed.  PASSPHRASE
may be NULL for the others.  A private key read is a private key with its
public part.  
.RE
.fi
.TP
int \fBgf_key_from_pem\fP (gf_key **out, const char *text, size_t len, const char *passphrase);
.TP
int \fBgf_key_to_pem_public\fP (const gf_key *key, char *out, size_t cap, size_t *len);
The "PUBLIC KEY" block (SPKI) for KEY, as openssl pkey \-pubout writes it. OUT is NUL\-terminated; *LEN receives its length without the NUL.
.SS "PuTTY"
.PP
A .ppk file of format 3, unencrypted or under AES\-256\-CBC with a key made by Argon2 (all three variants) of at most 512 MiB, 1000 passes and 16 lanes, with the MAC checked.  If COMMENT is not NULL it receives the file's comment as for RFC 4716.
.TP
int \fBgf_key_from_ppk\fP (gf_key **out, const char *text, size_t len, const char *passphrase, char *comment, size_t cap);
.SS "Picture"
.PP
The randomart image of the SHA\-256 fingerprint of KEY (a certificate has the one of the key it certifies), the one ssh\-keygen \-lv prints: eleven lines of 19 characters, each ending in a newline, the first and last being the border with the key type and size and "[SHA256]".  OUT is NUL\-terminated; *LEN receives its length without the NUL.  The least CAP is 221 (eleven lines of twenty bytes, and the NUL).
.TP
int \fBgf_key_randomart\fP (const gf_key *key, char *out, size_t cap, size_t *len);
